After creating the project and adding eureka server, spring web dependencies.
add this to the application.yml eureka: client: register-with-eureka: false ,fetch-registry: false
Normally, a Eureka Client tries to register itself with a Eureka Server.
But your Eureka Server is the registry itself. It doesn't make sense for it to register with itself.
So you tell it:
"Don't try to register yourself."
Hence: register-with-eureka: false
Again, the Eureka Server already owns the registry. It doesn't need to fetch it from anywhere else.
So: fetch-registry: false
Also enable the Eureka Server in your main application class with "@EnableEurekaServer".
By convention, Eureka Server runs on 8761 :Run it and verify that the Eureka dashboard opens at http://localhost:8761.